# Sales planning, step 7: totals

A sales plan is only useful if it tells you how you are doing against the target. The plan now adds up its deals: what has been won, what the open deals are likely to bring in, how many deals have been won, and the gap that is left.

Each total follows a path down through the plan's lists. `Clients.Deals.Value` means the value of every deal of every client, and the condition after the comma picks which deals count.

```bss
c DealStage
    Lead
    Qualified
    Proposal
    Negotiation
    Won
    Lost

c ActivityType
    Call
    Email
    Meeting

t SalesPlan|usl
    > A sales plan for a period: what you aim to sell, who you will sell it to, and how you are doing.
    s+                                                                     Name|Plan|e.g. "Sales Q4 2026"
    dd                                                                     StartDate|Starts|The first day of the period
    dd|(EndDate >= StartDate)                                              EndDate|Ends|The last day of the period
    n+|0..                                                                 Target|Target|How much you aim to sell in the period
    l:ucl                                                                  Clients|Clients|The people and companies you are selling to
    n=(sum(Clients.Deals.Value, Stage = Won))                              Won|Won|What you have sold so far
    n=(sum(Clients.Deals.WeightedValue, Stage != Won and Stage != Lost))   Forecast|Forecast|What you can expect from the deals that are still open
    i=(count(Clients.Deals, Stage = Won))                                  DealsWon|Deals Won|How many deals you have won
    n=(Target - Won)                                                       Gap|Gap to Target|What is still needed to reach the target

t Client|ucl
    > A person or company you are selling to.
    s+        Name|Client|The client's name
    r:tc      MainContact|Main Contact|The person you deal with
    l:udl     Deals|Deals|What you hope to sell them
    l:uac     Activities|Activities|Every call, email and meeting

t Deal|udl
    > Something you hope to sell to a client.
    s+                               Name|Deal|e.g. "Website redesign"
    n+|0..                           Value|Value|What the deal is worth
    DealStage=Lead                   Stage|Stage|How far the deal has got
    dd                               ExpectedClose|Expected Close|When you expect the client to decide
    i|0..100                         Probability|Probability (%)|How likely the deal is to be won
    n=(Value * Probability / 100)    WeightedValue|Weighted Value|What the deal is worth once its probability is taken into account
    l:ufu                            FollowUps|Follow-ups|The next steps

x FollowUp:TaskItem|ufu
    > A next step with a client, such as sending a proposal or a regular check-in call.
    s       Outcome|Outcome|What happened

t Activity|uac
    > A call, email or meeting with a client.
    s+                  Name|Activity|What it was about
    ActivityType=Call   Kind|Kind|Call, email or meeting
    d=now               Date|Date|When it happened
    r:tu=me             By|By|Who made the call, sent the email or went to the meeting
    s                   Outcome|Outcome|What came out of it
```
